rministic routing + full agent specs +\n13:   runtime policy + MCP + bootstrap. Agents are role specifications; **not yet**\n14:   wired as OpenCode subagents. Tribunal ported and self-contained; **live**\n15:   tribunal (semantic role execution) is **not** reachable until P4.\n16: - **v1.1** — planned: OpenCode subagents, dynamic role prompts, harness memory,\n17:   role contracts, native guard, live tribunal, plus reconciliation with the\n18:   canonical \"migration to plugin\" documentation (`патчи/миграция в плагин`,\n19:   TD-D* ledger). See `ROADMAP_v1.1.md` and `TECH_DEBT_AGENTS.md`.\n20: \n21: ## Layout\n22: \n23: ```\n24: .\n25: ├── .opencode/                    project-scoped OpenCode config (plugin + MCP)\n26: ├── agents/                       15 Harness subagents (orchestrators, workers, researcher, tribunal…)\n27: ├── config/                       runtime policy (runtime_snapshot.json, routes, guard_policy, …)\n28: ├── guard/                        doc_guard: session_guard.py, guard_runner.py, semantic_layer\n29: ├── mcp/                          bundled MCP servers (academic_search, coder_router, doc_extract, searxng)\n30: ├── packages/opencode-harness-plugin/   native OpenCode plugin bridge to Core (build -> dist/index.js)\n31: ├── scripts/                      router, orchestration, code-factory, researcher, writer-core\n32: ├── skills/opencode-current/      132 skills referenced by runtime routes\n33: ├── templates/                    reusable templates\n34: ├── AGENT_REPO_ACCESS.md          how an agent gets repo access from a new session\n35: └── deploy/                       bootstrap.ps1 (Windows) / bootstrap.sh (Linux/macOS)\n36: ```\n37: \n38: ## Quick start\n39: \n40: Windows:\n41: ```powershell\n42: cd opencode_harness_portable\n43: powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File deploy\\bootstrap.ps1\n44: ```\n45: \n46: Linux / macOS:\n47: ```bash\n48: cd opencode_harness_portable\n49: bash deploy/bootstrap.sh\n50: ```\n51: \n52: Bootstrap will:\n53: 1. Create `.venv` (Python 3.11+) and install requirements.\n54: 2. Build the native plugin (`npm run build` -> `dist/index.js`).\n55: 3. Install project plugin deps (`@opencode-ai/plugin`).\n56: 4. Register the plugin in `.opencode/opencode.json` (file:// URI, project-scoped).\n57: 5. Recompile the runtime policy snapshot (`compile_runtime.py`).\n58: 6. Write `.env`.\n59: 7. Run `doctor.py` and `health_check.py`.\n60: \n61: Then **open this folder in OpenCode Desktop**. The plugin loads automatically.\n62: \n63: ## Verify\n64: \n65: - Log marker on load: `harness plugin loaded protocol=harness-bridge-rpc/1.0 required_features_ok=true`\n66: - Chat tools: `harness_status` (readiness) and `harness_run` (deterministic routing).\n67: \n68: ## Requirements\n69: \n70: - Python 3.11+ (auto-detected, or set `PYTHON_BIN`)\n71: - Node.js + npm (for plugin build; a prebuilt `dist/` can be shipped instead)\n72: - OpenCode Desktop 1.18.30+ (tested)\n73: \n74: ## Notes\n75: \n76: - Never load the legacy `plugins/tool-skill-contract-router.ts` alongside the native plugin.\n77: - All paths are resolved relative to the repo root (`OPENCODE_HARNESS_ROOT` auto-detected).\n78: - Secrets belong in `.env` (git-ignored), never in committed configs."}], "metadata": {"truncated": false}}, "time": {"created": 1791912672248, "ran": 1791912672255, "completed": 1791912672324}}, {"type": "tool", "id": "call_XprxBGDhFsUyhRJCZozbGjOa", "name": "shell", "executed": false, "providerState": {"itemId": "fc_0f05ab37e548106a016ace6ae75a9887d29c080e36da6b9245"}, "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "git status --short; git rev-parse --show-toplevel", "workdir": "E:\\opencode_harness_portable"}, "content": [{"type": "text", "text": " M config/agent_categories/article-writer.json\n M config/agent_categories/claim-parser.json\n M config/agent_categories/code-auditor.json\n M config/agent_categories/code-orchestrator.json\n M config/agent_categories/code-reviewer.json\n M config/agent_cat